  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Illinois received $10.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Federal contract activity included 435,867 awards with an average award size of $23.2K. Obligations are down 18.5% year over year. Annual obligations reached $13.6B in FY22 and trended between $12B and $13.4B from FY21 through FY25 before the FY26 to date total of $10.1B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer in the state with $5.2B in obligations, followed by the Department of Energy with $1.8B and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $1.7B. Medical and research industries lead by dollar value, with Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences each at $1.1B. Vendors with the largest obligations include W S DARLEY & CO at $1.2B and UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC at $1.1B. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have federal obligations in Illinois changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Illinois obligations peaked at $13.6B in FY22 and stayed above $12B through FY25, including $13B in FY23 and $13.4B in FY24. Illinois obligations were $12B in FY21 and $12.4B in FY25. Illinois obligations are $10.1B in FY26 to date. Obligations are down 18.5% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in Illinois?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense leads with $5.2B in obligations, followed by the Department of Energy with $1.8B and the Department of Veterans Affairs with $1.7B. W S DARLEY & CO and UCHICAGO ARGONNE, LLC are the top vendors with $1.2B and $1.1B respectively, and MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP follows at $859M. Medical equipment wholesalers and research and development sectors each account for $1.1B in obligations, making those industries the largest by dollar value."
      }
    ]
  },
